<title>UK: Hamleys chief executive quits.</title>
<headline>Hamleys chief executive quits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hamleys Plc, the massive toy shop on Regent Street in London's central shopping district, said on Thursday its chief executive Geoff Cullinan has resigned to pursue other business interests.  </p>
<p>The company said Cullinan would stay on for a period while Hamleys looked for a replacement.</p>
<p>The group also reported an 18 percent jump in first half pretax profits to two million stg. This included a 17 percent rise in profits from its flagship store on Regent Street in the heart of London's West End shopping district.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
